   866	  [review](proposals/MERGED.md)). It
   867	  supersedes the pipeline of [VERIFIED_PIPELINE.md](../legacy/docs/compiler/VERIFIED_PIPELINE.md).
   868	  The slice-0 design (`Concrete/README.md`, on branch `wip/slice0`) becomes the detailed
   869	  description once it lands.
   870	  - *Stages.* Bytes → lexer → LL(1) parser (the grammar is data, with a mechanical LL(1) check) →
   871	    AST → resolve → HIR (the resolved surface only) → elaboration → Core → checker → CheckedCore
   872	    (the single admission point, with its certificate and discharged-evidence tokens; admission
   873	    is re-checked after Mono) → Mono Core → Place MIR (which only expands residual checks) →
   874	    Memory CFG (layout, ABI, byte and provenance memory) → SSA → BIR. BIR is a complete backend
   875	    contract: layout, endianness, calling convention, trap kind and site, and the frame-accounting
   876	    handoff.
   877	  - *Backends.* From BIR, an unverified LLVM printer, and the BIR → LCB-IR adapter (the first
   878	    backend proof) feeding the Lean Compiler Backend on AArch64, proved later. Both run from slice
   879	    0, and CI compares their full observations ([backend order](#decided-project-proof-infrastructure)).
   880	  - *Proof per stage.* Direct proofs for the lexer and parser (a correspondence theorem), resolve
   881	    and elaboration, sequencing, cleanup, representation lowering and BIR → LCB-IR. Proved
   882	    validators for Mono, SSA (a direct proof is allowed in slice 0), optimizations, register
   883	    allocation and linking. After slice 0, per-edge certificates replace the whole-compiler
   884	    `decide` certificate (R-0582, R-0583).
   885	  - *The theorem.* The end-to-end theorem has named premises, with the LLVM and LCB premises
   886	    separate; the holes only shrink.
   887	  - *One evidence graph.* Facts, diagnostics and source sites come from one evidence graph with
   888	    typed site identities.
