   966	  - *Stack bounds.* From slice 0, `concrete facts` reports each program's maximum stack use,
   967	    measured from the final binary on both backends. An unknown bound, or one over the
   968	    `Concrete.toml` stack budget, is refused, so stack overflow is never a hidden trap. Slice 5
   969	    (recursion) extends it with proven bounds.
