  1166	- <a id="decided-2026-11-08-language"></a>**Language and process decisions of 2026-11-08** (owner,
  1167	  2026-11-08: "record, yes to all recommended", approving the list as recommended; "i prefer fully
  1168	  gone, self and as are irrelevant from what i see", on `self` and `as`; and "i like 3", on how
  1169	  imported items are used). Codex, Kimi and agy reviewed the list in six rounds and agreed on every
  1170	  item except 11(b), which the owner then decided by choosing option 3. The spellings of items 6–29
  1171	  and 40–53 are illustrative; their exact spellings come in the [spelling round](#decided-2026-11-08-spelling-round).
  1172	  The trap names (item 4) and the grammar items 30–39 are decided as written.
  1173	  The numbers are the list's.
  1174	  - <a id="decided-2026-11-08-process"></a>*Process.*
  1175	    1. *Sign-off when the review cap is reached.* The owner may approve one exact SHA after Codex,
  1176	       Kimi and agy have all reviewed it. The approval and every outstanding finding and verdict
  1177	       are recorded. It never replaces a gate or a proof obligation.
  1178	    2. *A diff that touches several classes* gets the highest of their caps (docs 2, scripts 3,
  1179	       compiler and spec 5), classified by the files the diff actually changes. This settles the
  1180	       question [review caps](#decided-2026-11-08-review-caps) left to the owner.
  1181	    3. *One review round on where each std item lives* ([std per slice](#decided-2026-11-08-std-table)).
  1182	    4. *Trap names:* `overflow`, `division_by_zero`, `invalid_shift`, `out_of_bounds`,
  1183	       `invalid_range` and `abort`. They are diagnostic categories, distinct from the error types
  1184	       of the checked operations. This answers [foundation question 9](#foundation-q9).
  1185	    5. *Slice 0 lands at `0e2950e7`*, which three reviewers accepted with CI 9/9 green.
  1186	  - *Language simplifications.*
  1187	    6. *No dot method calls:* a call is `Type::f(x)` or `Trait::f(x)`.
  1188	    7. *No receiver forms:* `self`, `&self` and `&mut self` are replaced by an ordinary typed first
  1189	       parameter. One consuming `Destroy` protocol is kept.
  1190	    8. *Constructors* always write `field: value`.
  1191	    9. *Patterns* always write `field: binder`. The rules for ignored fields and linear
  1192	       consumption are kept.
  1193	    10. *Contracts mark exact mathematical arithmetic explicitly.* Its spelling and scope come
  1194	        later; [OD12](#od12) and [OD145](#od145) are kept.
  1195	    11. *`as` is removed from the language entirely*, and is not reserved.
  1196	        - (a) Expression casts are replaced by one canonical named lossless conversion. The
  1197	          value-domain rule of [OD11](#od11) and its provenance restrictions are kept.
  1198	        - (b) <a id="decided-2026-11-08-imports-qualified"></a>Import renaming is removed. Every
  1199	          imported item is always qualified (option 3; round-6 reviewers: Codex 3, Kimi 3, agy 1).
  1200	          - Imports stay item lists (`import std::json::{parse};`); the MOD-2 manifest and
  1201	            [OD139](#od139) are kept.
  1202	          - Every imported item is used as `<last segment of its module>::name` everywhere: in
  1203	            values, types, patterns and theorem paths (`json::parse(...)`, `vec::Vec<u8>`). It is
  1204	            never used bare.
  1205	          - Items declared in the same module, and builtin types, stay bare.
  1206	          - Two items with the same name from different modules may both be imported.
  1207	          - Two imported modules with the same last segment are refused.
  1208	          - A local named like an imported segment is refused; there is no shadowing.
  1209	        - (c) Borrowing is written `borrow [mut] view = source [from a until b] { ... } [else { ... }]`.
  1210	        - (d) Unpacking is written `unpack <brand A> x = p { ... }`.
  1211	    12. *Heap move-out:* the consuming `*h` on a heap box is replaced by one named move-out
  1212	        operation. It keeps allocator identity and conservation, and stays distinct from
  1213	        destruction.
  1214	    13. *`assert(e);`* is always parenthesized, with an optional `by` suffix.
  1215	    14. *Symbol attributes* are written `#[link_name("sym")]` and `#[export_name("sym")]`.
  1216	    15. *Import paths* use `::`.
  1217	    16. *No `char`:* text is `u8` plus explicit UTF-8 operations. Quoted ASCII literals, patterns
  1218	        and comparisons migrate explicitly.
  1219	    17. *No `print`, `println` or `append` builtins.* Output is an ordinary call that needs
  1220	        `Console` and its grant, and its linear errors are kept. String append is an ordinary
  1221	        allocating operation under `with(Alloc)`, not `Console`.
  1222	    18. *Written types:* every local has a written type, and every function a result arrow,
  1223	        `-> Unit` included. Generic arguments are still inferred from the call's arguments. The
  1224	        typing rules for destructuring and ghost bindings are defined later (item 55).
  1225	  - *Removals and keeps.*
  1226	    19. *`OrderedMap` only, for now.* `HashMap` comes when the key-value store's measurements
  1227	        (slice 23) need it. Map names get no compiler privilege.
  1228	    20. *`Process`:* every foreign declaration is audited first; the capability is removed only
  1229	        if none needs it ([authority rules](#decided-2026-11-02-authority)).
  1230	    21. *`defer` is kept with late reads* (Q9.8). Reserved by-value arguments, held loans
  1231	        and cleanup order are kept.
  1232	    22. *Handwritten bodyless ordinary functions are refused.* Compiler-generated interfaces
  1233	        ([OD9](#od9), [OD39](#od39)) keep bodyless declarations, as do trait signatures and
  1234	        `extern`.
  1235	    23. *No packed structs* until a real packed foreign ABI needs them. A demonstrated ABI
  1236	        reopens the question.
  1237	    24. *Local `assume`* is removed only after its replacement, named trusted contracts with
  1238	        evidence identity, has been shown on real examples, point-local conditional facts
  1239	        included. Until then it stays explicit and tracked, and it never admits a safety
  1240	        obligation.
  1241	    25. *Function values* keep the decided design: a function pointer plus explicit context, with
  1242	        contracts.
  1243	    26. *Constants are computed at compile time*, and a constant's value must be `Copy`. Before
  1244	        Q6.4 and TYPE-22 are revised, the closed total subset of initializers is defined and the
  1245	        decided conditions for reopening compile-time evaluation are checked.
  1246	    27. *Kept explicitly:* value-producing `if` and `match`, both proof scopes, and existential
  1247	        brands.
  1248	    28. *SPARK 4(b):* an optional `#[depends(result <- a, b)]`, checked against the derived fact and
  1249	        never trusted.
  1250	    29. *SPARK 4(c):* a dead store to a `mut` local is refused, extending [OD62](#od62).
  1251	  - *Grammar*, under the grammar review's own numbering (`OPEN-n` there, not the open items of this
  1252	    file).
  1253	    30. *Source text (OPEN-1):* UTF-8 source. Whitespace is space, tab, LF and CR. A `//` comment
  1254	        ends at LF, CR or end of file. There are no block comments, BOM, shebang or NUL.
  1255	    31. *Identifiers (OPEN-2)* are ASCII and case-sensitive.
  1256	    32. *Builtin names (OPEN-4):* one closed table of builtin names, with no aliases.
  1257	    33. *Escapes (OPEN-6):* exactly two escape lists, and no raw line breaks in quotes.
  1258	    34. *Tokens (OPEN-7):* longest match. `>>` is split only in generic closers.
  1259	    35. *Aliases and constants (OPEN-10):* `type N = T;` and `const N: T = e;`.
  1260	    36. *Attributes (OPEN-15):* a closed attribute set.
  1261	    37. *`borrow` and `defer` (OPEN-19):* the restrictions as proposed.
  1262	    38. *Views and constant-time APIs (OPEN-21)* are ordinary calls.
  1263	    39. *Concurrency (OPEN-24):* no concurrency syntax until the model is reviewed.
  1264	    40. *Reserved words (OPEN-3):* `spec`, `by`, `kept`, `Self`, `while` and `Entropy`. `self`
  1265	        and `as` are not reserved: they are ordinary identifiers with no special meaning, and
  1266	        Rust-style `&self` or `x as u32` gets an ordinary parse or resolution error, not a
  1267	        dedicated diagnostic. Obsolete reservations (`in`, `newtype`, `union`, `total`) are dropped
  1268	        unless a decided row still needs them.
  1269	    41. *Number suffixes (OPEN-5):* typed suffixes like `200u8` are kept; the exact suffix
  1270	        grammar comes later.
  1271	    42. *Precedence (OPEN-8):* the legacy precedence table is kept, so chained comparisons parse.
  1272	        agy preferred refusing chains.
  1273	    43. *Item syntax (OPEN-9):* attributes, then `pub`, then the item. Commas are mandatory, and a
  1274	        trailing comma is optional.
  1275	    44. *Imports (OPEN-11):* `import a::b::{x, y};` with a nonempty item list. There is no renaming
  1276	        and no module import, which all three reviewers rejected as a second form against the MOD-2
  1277	        manifest. Uses follow 11(b).
  1278	    45. *Spec functions (OPEN-13):* `spec fn f(...) -> T = e;` and `assert(e) by path(args);`. Spec
  1279	        functions use a pure subset, and the name restriction on `ghost let` is fixed.
  1280	    46. *Generic parameters (OPEN-14):* type parameters come before capability parameters (`cap C`).
  1281	        Unions use `+`, and `{}` is empty. Capability names are never ordinary types.
  1282	    47. *Blocks (OPEN-16):* the decided statement and value block behaviour is kept, with the
  1283	        common-prefix LL(1) grammar proved.
  1284	    48. *Match (OPEN-17):* enum patterns are qualified, and every arm ends with a comma.
  1285	    49. *Labels (OPEN-18):* both loop forms take labels (`'label: while`, `'label: for`), with
  1286	        `break 'label;` and `continue 'label;`. There are no empty statements.
  1287	    50. *Arrays (OPEN-20):* no empty array literals; empty structs are kept.
  1288	    51. *Brands (OPEN-22):* an explicit `exists`/`pack`/`unpack` brand surface, and named binder
  1289	        contracts on function types.
  1290	    52. *Kept arguments (OPEN-23):* `kept buf: H`, with its paired `Kept<H>` completion, and no
  1291	        borrow-derived kept arguments (Q3.12 in full). Only pointer qualification is left.
  1292	    53. *Ratified (OPEN-25):* value `while ... else` and postfix member `->` stay refused.
  1293	  - *Later, with no decision now.*
  1294	    54. The Core freeze (A2c), after the spec-core proofs and A2i integration.
  1295	    55. <a id="decided-2026-11-08-spelling-round"></a>*The spelling round:* the exact names and
  1296	        signatures of the lossless conversion, the move-out, the mathematical-arithmetic boundary,
  1297	        output and append, and the typing rules for destructuring and ghost bindings, together
  1298	        with every spelling from items 6–29 and 40–53. They are shown to the owner as before/after code.
  1299	    56. The entropy grant's shape, at slice 6.
  1300	    57. The concurrency model, at slice 28.
  1301	    58. Niches and smaller enum tags, only if a workload needs them.
  1302	    59. The remaining open grammar sub-rules come back to the owner in the spelling round with
  1303	        item 55, as before/after code:
  1304	        - the numeric token policy (OPEN-5);
  1305	        - attribute duplication, ordering
, attachment and scope, the struct-invariant scope
  1306	          included (OPEN-15);
  1307	        - zero-count array repetition (OPEN-20);
  1308	        - the closed builtin inventory, and exhaustive signatures for the view, constant-time,
  1309	          text, container and branded APIs (OPEN-4/21);
  1310	        - trait and inherent impl shells (OPEN-12);
  1311	        - brand binder scope, escape and loop-carried existential rules (OPEN-22).
  1312	  - <a id="decided-2026-11-08-language-revisions"></a>*Rows this revises*, each an explicit owner
